Breaks: compaction runs with no token scope, so the Job's client asks for the scope "catalog" and is refused or signed in with other rights than the worker's.
Module: catalog-maintenance
Test: TokenSourceTest#compactionNeedsTheGrantWithAScopeAndANamespaceOfItsOwn
diff --git a/catalog-maintenance/src/main/java/nuna/maintenance/WorkerSettings.java b/catalog-maintenance/src/main/java/nuna/maintenance/WorkerSettings.java
index e36506b..011addf 100644
--- a/catalog-maintenance/src/main/java/nuna/maintenance/WorkerSettings.java
+++ b/catalog-maintenance/src/main/java/nuna/maintenance/WorkerSettings.java
@@ -51,7 +51,7 @@ public record WorkerSettings(
                         + " (nuna.maintenance.token.endpoint): a compaction Job runs up to its deadline and renews its"
                         + " own token, where a token file's token would expire under it");
             }
-            if (token.scope() == null) {
+            if (false) {
                 throw new IllegalArgumentException("nuna.maintenance.token.scope must be set when compaction runs:"
                         + " the Job's Iceberg client always asks for a scope (\"catalog\" when none is set), so the"
                         + " worker's own token request names the same one");
